---
description: Rust conventions
globs: **/*.rs,**/Cargo.toml
alwaysApply: false
---
- Keep `cargo fmt` and `cargo clippy -- -D warnings` clean.
- Use `Result` and `?`; libraries use `thiserror`, binaries may use `anyhow`. No `unwrap()`/`expect()` outside tests unless an invariant is documented.
- Prefer borrowing over cloning; justify every `clone()` on a hot path.
- Every `unsafe` block gets a `// SAFETY:` comment stating the invariant it relies on.
- Unit tests in the same file under `#[cfg(test)]`, integration tests in `tests/`.
